    {
      "name": "D7",
      "label": "GPIO7 (Button)",
      "codeName": "D7",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_input",
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "button"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_BUTTON / BOOT — onboard bootloader-select pushbutton, also usable as a general input when application code is running. Active-low with the RP2040's internal pull-up enabled (no external pull-up on this line). Confirmed via Zephyr's adafruit_feather_scorpio_rp2040.dts gpio_keys node (gpios = <&gpio0 7 (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW | GPIO_PULL_UP)>) and Adafruit's own pinouts guide (\"BOOT (aka digital pin 7 in Arduino) can be used as an input if you don't want to wire up a button on another pin\"). Full digital_input/digital_output/pwm_output capability retained (ordinary GPIO wired to a switch to GND, not a dedicated/capacitive-only pin), matching this repo's vccgnd_yd_rp2040 PIN_USRKEY precedent."
    },
    {
