    {
      "name": "D13",
      "label": "GPIO13 (Led active high)",
      "codeName": "D13",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_high"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED — onboard status LED, active-high. Confirmed via Zephyr's adafruit_feather_scorpio_rp2040.dts leds node (gpios = <&gpio0 13 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>), consistent with Adafruit's own pinouts guide describing it as controllable via digital pin 13 and pulsing in bootloader mode. digital_input dropped to match this repo's established led_high precedent for dedicated onboard LED pins (rpipico, wiznet_5500_evb_pico, vccgnd_yd_rp2040); pwm_output kept since arduino-pico's analogWrite() works on any RP2040 GPIO, enabling brightness dimming. This GPIO was also the vendor's default (unused) PIN_SPI0_SS alias, which would have contaminated this confirmed LED tag with a spurious spi_ss capability - fixed 2026-07-12 by removing that alias from pins_arduino.h (no onboard SPI device consumes it), matching the ESP32/ESP8266 audit's bus-alias-contamination fix pattern (see project_board_variant_pin_audit_playbook section 12)."
    },
